        {
          "type": "turn_end",
          "turn": {
            "text": "Alberto's Fraud Detection Agent is built for an online event ticketing platform. It reviews newly published events and organizers, then gives a human admin an approve, reject, or request-info recommendation along with its reasons.\n\nIt uses graded autonomy: it auto-approves only when the evidence is verified in code, and web sources can hold a decision back but can never approve one.\n\nThe project is currently in offline evals, on 31 cases:\n- On a local 9B model, approved fraud fell from 54% to 8% over twelve iterations, and fraud approved without a human fell from 27% to 0%.\n- For deployment, Claude Haiku 5.5 was chosen. It reached 86% accuracy versus 71% for the local model, and 1% of fraud was approved versus 8%. It costs about $0.002 per review. Haiku's figures are the mean of 3 runs; the local model had 1 run.\n\nThe stack is TypeScript, PostgreSQL and GCP.",
